%% Trade-off map of every connectivity control available on this project - how private it actually makes the traffic against what it costs to build and run
%% Source: Microsoft Learn - Azure Storage firewall rules and network access (IP rules need Microsoft peering NAT addresses, service endpoints keep traffic on the public IP), Configure Azure File Sync network endpoints (no service endpoint option for File Sync), Private endpoints overview for Azure Backup (Azure Files backup does not need them), ExpressRoute circuits and peering; codex/blueprint-azure-files-private-endpoint.md, codex/blueprint-azure-file-sync-private-path.md
quadrantChart
  title Connectivity controls for Contoso file workloads
  x-axis "Traffic still lands on a public IP" --> "Traffic stays on private IPs end to end"
  y-axis "Cheap to build and run" --> "Expensive to build and run"
  quadrant-1 "Private and costly - Contoso target, budget it once"
  quadrant-2 "Costly and still public - never worth it here"
